{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.KazhdanLusztigBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KazhdanLusztigBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.bar_smul_self_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.bar_smul_self_iff","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L171-L190","doc":"**The scalar-multiple form of KL self-duality.** `r • C w` is bar-invariant\nexactly when `r` is fixed by `barR`.\n\n`Nontrivial R` is needed for the forward direction — over the zero ring\nevery element is `0` and the statement is empty, which is the ring-level\nanalogue of the vacuity this module exists to prevent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.bar_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.bar_smul","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L155-L169","doc":"**Bar-invariance is not automatic, and this says exactly when it holds.**\n\n`barM` fixes the basis but is *semilinear*, so it does not fix the module:\non `r • C w` it acts by `barR r`. The scalar multiple is bar-invariant\nprecisely when the scalar is fixed by `barR`.\n\nThis is the content that `KLBasisElt : Type u` had no room to express — with\nno bar and no basis, \"bar-invariant\" was not a condition on anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.nontrivial_of_klBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.nontrivial_of_klBasis","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L144-L153","doc":"**The anti-`PUnit` theorem, and the reason this file exists.**\n\nA module carrying a KL basis indexed by a nonempty `W` is nontrivial. So\n`KLBasisElt := PUnit` — the value the retired `canonical` instance used to\ndischarge `conj:kazhdan-lusztig-classical-limit` — cannot inhabit this\nstructure, and a downstream class that requires a `KLBasis` is stating a\nconstraint rather than a signature anything satisfies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.basis_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.basis_injective","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L139-L142","doc":"Distinct group elements give distinct basis elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L135-L137","doc":"Every KL basis element is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L128-L128","doc":"Kazhdan–Lusztig self-duality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.basis","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The basis itself, indexed by the group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.KLBasis","kind":"structure","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L106-L128","doc":"**A Kazhdan–Lusztig basis, as a specification.**\n\n`basis` is the substantive field: a KL basis is a *basis*, indexed by the\nCoxeter group. That single requirement is what `KLBasisElt : Type u` was\nmissing, and it is what rules out `PUnit`.\n\n`bar_invariant` is the KL self-duality `\\overline{C_w} = C_w`, the property\nthat (together with degree-bounded unitriangularity against the `T`-basis)\ncharacterises the basis uniquely.\n\n**Not included: unitriangularity.** `C_w = T_w + Σ_{v < w} P_{v,w} T_v` with\n`deg P_{v,w} ≤ (ℓ(w) − ℓ(v) − 1)/2` needs the `T`-basis and the Bruhat\norder, i.e. the Hecke algebra this tree does not have. Its absence is why\nthis is a specification of what a KL basis *satisfies* rather than a\ncharacterisation that pins it: two different bar-invariant bases both\ninhabit `KLBasis`. Downstream may therefore use this to *constrain*, never\nto conclude uniqueness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.IsBarFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.IsBarFixed","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L100-L102","doc":"The scalars fixed by `barR` form a subring; membership is the predicate that\ndecides bar-invariance of a scalar multiple (`bar_smul_self_iff`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L96-L98","doc":"`barM` is bijective — an involution always is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_barM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_barM","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L93-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barR_barR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barR_barR","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L90-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_smul","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Semilinearity: `bar` twists scalars by `barR`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_invol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM_invol","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L82-L82","doc":"…which is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barM","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The involution on the module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barR_invol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barR_invol","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L78-L78","doc":"…which is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.barR","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The involution on scalars — `q ↦ q⁻¹` in the motivating case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.KL.BarInvolution","kind":"structure","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/KazhdanLusztigBasis.lean#L63-L84","doc":"**A bar involution.**\n\nSemilinearity is written out (`barM_smul`) rather than routed through\nMathlib's `σ`-semilinear maps, because the only thing needed downstream is\nthe compatibility equation itself and the `LinearMap.semilinear` route would\nforce a `RingHomInvPair` instance for a ring map that is only involutive.\n\nFor the QOU ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` this is `q ↦ q⁻¹`; nothing here\ndepends on that, and the structure is stated over an arbitrary `CommRing` so\nthe §7c base-ring wall is respected. ","signatureChunk":0}]}